Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To clarify which objects are part of the lockout zone, you might, for example, insert a Cuboid into the
Frame and assign a Material to it. Proceed as follows:
• Click the Cuboid on the ribbon tab Edit. Type in a small value for the Dimension Z, the height of the
Cuboid.
• Insert the Cuboid above Station2 and press the M key to show the manipulators.
• Click the bottom right corner of the Cuboid and drag it, so that it covers the LockoutZone and the
Stations.
Specify the Stations Which the LockoutZone Stops
Plant Simulation Help 10-573
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• As our Cuboid overlaps the captions of the objects, we move it, so that they become visible. Select
Station1, press the spacebar and change to the tab Captions in the dialog Edit 3D Properties. We
selected -1.35 as the Y position for the three affected Stations.
• We finally have to adjust the position of the caption of the LockoutZone and assign a Material/color to
the Cuboid.
